{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The cost properties are optional on purpose: they arrive flat, and a field that does not apply","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the named function is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"absent, not zero","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". Reading a missing ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stretch at the wrong cost and fail against a record that is perfectly good (§23.4 rule 5).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These are never cached across exchanges and never defaulted locally. A credential enrolled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under one cost keeps working after a tenant raises its policy, so a client that guessed would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derive a different randomized password and report “invalid password” for one that is entirely","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"correct (§23.4 rule 2).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"This is where Swift stopped needing a `pbkdf2_sha256` tenant","type":"heading","anchor":"This-is-where-Swift-stopped-needing-a-pbkdf2sha256-tenant"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SRP client this replaces refused an ","type":"text"},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tenant outright: Swift has no Argon2 that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ships on every supported platform, and substituting PBKDF2 would have derived a different ","type":"text"},{"code":"x","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and surfaced as “invalid password”. AXIAM’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" KDF was, for Swift, unreachable. The key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stretching now happens inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"libaxiam_opaque_ffi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is no longer a Swift-shaped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hole — and ","type":"text"},{"code":"pbkdf2_sha256","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not an OPAQUE key-stretching function at all.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/ksfparams"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The key-stretching function and cost a ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" response names (CONTRACT.md §23.4).","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK9KsfParamsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KsfParams","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"KsfParams"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/init(ksf:memoryKib:iterations:parallelism:logN:r:p:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/iterations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/ksf","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/logN","doc:\/\/Axiam